    "result_text": "Claim reassignment is built, but `bin/e2e` is not fully green: 3 of the 4 tests pass. Scenario 3 fails on a step that runs before any reassign and has nothing to do with this change.\n\n**Why scenario 3 fails (`acceptance.spec.ts:523`):** the step is `editPerson(Ada, grade B, from 2026-03-20)`, run while the sheet's today is 2026-03-10. The app saves the edit, but Ada's row keeps showing grade A, because the grade starts on a later date. The test waits for the row to show B, so it times out after 8 seconds. The test's expected audit line for the same edit, `PERSON_EDITED \u2026 grade=A`, doesn't fit that wait: if the row showed B, the app would log `grade=B`. No single behaviour satisfies both, so I left the existing grade logic alone rather than bend it to the test.\n\nTo check the reassign part of scenario 3, I ran a temporary copy of it that skips that wait and corrects the one audit line. Everything else passed, including the `CLAIM_REASSIGNED \u2026 from=Cam to=Ada` line. I deleted that copy afterwards; the real spec is unchanged.\n\n**What the change does:**\n- **Server** (`ClaimService.reassign`, endpoint `POST /api/sheets/{id}/claims/{claimId}/reassign`):\n  - Only a steward can move a claim, and only a DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING one.\n  - The claim keeps its number and date. Any figure a statement bound it to is cleared, so it's live again until its new person's next statement.\n  - It writes `CLAIM_REASSIGNED`, naming the new person, with ` from=<old> to=<new>` at the end. The usual person and sheet total lines follow when totals change.\n- **Refusals I added that the request didn't spell out**, to match how other claim actions behave:\n  - moving to the person it already belongs to\n  - moving to a person retired by the claim's date\n  - moving a claim dated in a closed period\n  - moving a correction (a negative amount) to someone who doesn't have the settled claim it corrects\n- **Front end** (`person-claims.ts`, `claims.service.ts`): each claim row has a person picker (`claim-reassign-to`) listing everyone else on the sheet, retired people included, and a Move button (`claim-reassign`). A refusal shows in `claim-error`, which clears on the next action on that row.",
